# Review: ZenPlugin

The data model, mixer engine, binaural generator, sample player, countdown with linear fade-out and
the Mixer/Sound/Editor components are all built and match the spec closely. Apart from the sleep fade, nothing is
tested beyond module activation, so every other implemented item is `untested` and every scenario `missing`.
Two divergences come from one design choice: `MixerEngine.updateLayer` rebuilds a layer on every
change, so neither live AudioParam ramps (F-4.4) nor in-place sample muting (F-5.3) happen, though
the generator and player both have code for them.

Of 39 items: 3 done, 25 untested, 0 partial, 2 diverged, 9 missing. Only the sleep fade (F-6) is
tested, by unit tests of `timedPlaybackStep` and of `MixerEngine` against a fake AudioContext. Findings:

- **Few behavioural tests.** Only `MixerEngine.fadeOut`/`stop` and `timedPlaybackStep` are tested; layer
  playback, `BinauralGenerator` and `useCountdown` could be tested the same way and are not.
- **F-4.4 diverged.** `BinauralGenerator.setConfig` (ramped) is never called; changes restart the layer.
- **F-5.3 diverged.** Mute stops the sample node instead of setting its gain to zero.

